---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const privacyEmail = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_EMAIL?.trim() || 'privacy@anchor.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="How Anchor uses cookies and similar storage, and how to change your choice."
  currentPath="/cookies"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We keep cookies and local storage to a minimum. Contact <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a> with
      questions.
    </p>

    <h2>Essential</h2>
    <p>
      Telegram Login keeps a short-lived <code>id_token</code> in <code>sessionStorage</code> as{' '}
      <code>anchor_telegram_id_token</code> while this browser tab is open. The consent banner preference is stored under{' '}
      <code>anchor-consent-v1</code> in <code>localStorage</code>. Accessibility display settings from the Accessibility
      button are stored under <code>anchor-a11y-prefs-v1</code> in <code>localStorage</code> on this device only.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics / marketing</h2>
    <p>We do not set analytics or marketing cookies by default in this prototype.</p>

    <h2>Change your choice</h2>
    <p>
      Clear site data for this domain in your browser, or remove <code>anchor-consent-v1</code> from local storage, then
      reload to see the banner again. Closing the tab clears the Telegram sign-in token.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
